{
 "id": "ph_warm_earth",
 "title": "The Warm Earth",
 "kind": "hero",
 "seed": 5101,
 "intro": [
  "For three hundred years Ysmay Vane has ruled the fens of Sallowmere from a throne no one else wanted: a dwindling court of the dead, too few to matter. This autumn the ground is warm, and the dead are waking by the thousand. They crawl up out of the mud as if something below were chasing them.",
  "A court that grows can be a kingdom. Ysmay sends her champion, Sir Orrin Wren, a hundred years in his grave, to tell the barrow-lords of the fen. Vathek of Cairnholt answers that he kneels to no one.",
  "How to play: right click to walk and fight, right click someone to talk. A gold ! means they want something, a ? means you can report back. Q, W, E and R use Ysmay's skills; K opens her skill trees. If she falls she wakes at the last shrine she touched.",
  "Go down to the Weeping Mere and see the risen for yourself. Then take Vathek's word back from Cairnholt."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "vathek_bound"
   },
   "text": [
    "Vathek's hill falls and his dead turn to the Regent without a word. They were never his; they were only near him. His skull rides at Ysmay's belt now, and mutters at night about the heat.",
    "Ysmay counts what she has gained and finds the number is still rising. Every night more of the dead climb out of the fen, and none of them can say what woke them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
    "Vathek's hill falls and his dead turn to the Regent without a word. They were never his; they were only near him.",
    "Ysmay counts what she has gained and finds the number is still rising. Every night more of the dead climb out of the fen, and none of them can say what woke them."
   ]
  }
